// @run
// @log 3
// @log ab
// CONTRACT (must-RUN): a union of a string LITERAL and a scalar is the boxed value union
// `string|i32` once the emitter softens the literal (`canonEmitName`: "a mixed-base union
// keeps each softened member"), so `print` lowers it exactly as it lowers the
// already-softened spelling `string | i32` (tests/cases/types/print-union-runs.vl) — a tag
// test per arm, and the arm the value holds is printed.
//
// TWO EARLIER STATES, BOTH WRONG IN DIFFERENT WAYS. Before D-LITPRINT the two spellings
// DISAGREED: `string | i32` was a clean reject while `"ab" | i32` walked past the gate and
// built a module that failed to parse as WebAssembly (`type mismatch: expected i32, found
// (ref $type)`) — the gate classified each leaf with `retAtomKindOf`, which answers -1 for a
// literal, and one -1 leaf declined the whole union. D-LITPRINT made them agree by refusing
// both; D712 makes them agree by BUILDING both.
const v: "ab" | i32 = 3
print(v)

const s: "ab" | i32 = "ab"
print(s)
